        "citations": ["Two popular swarm algorithms used in search are particle swarm optimization (inspired by bird flocking) and ant colony optimization (inspired by ant trails)."]
    },
    {
        "question": "What is the common sense knowledge problem that early natural language processing work faced?",
        "answer": "Early natural language processing work, based on Noam Chomsky's generative grammar and semantic networks, had difficulty with word-sense disambiguation unless restricted to small domains called 'micro-worlds' due to the common sense knowledge problem.",
        "estimated_difficulty": 6,
        "citations": ["Early work, based on Noam Chomsky's generative grammar and semantic networks, had difficulty with word-sense disambiguation[f] unless restricted to small domains called \"micro-worlds\" (due to the common sense knowledge problem)."]
    },
